Amplify awareness! Amplify context!

This is one of the [[Permacomputing]] principles. Hannah Gmeiner's thesis puts it this way:

<<<
Originally, computers were invented to support cognitive processes with the goal of "intelligence amplification." However, intelligence can be applied narrowly and blindly, making it more advantageous to focus on amplifying awareness instead.
<<< Hannah Gmeiner, //Permacomputing as a Practice for Digital Graphic Design//

She defines awareness as "understanding the current state of the world and the environment and knowing how things function within their various contexts—cultural, historical, biological, and more." It means observing a technology and also placing it in what surrounds it.

The opposite habit is [[Virtualism]], which hides the context. [[Signs Signaling Sustainability]] is one way to do the amplifying.